  "description": "BUSKEH crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C70 H91 Ho5 O21 S4,C1 H4 O1,3(C1 H2 Cl2),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho5 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.517-5.007 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.30-169.14°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ho5(μ4-OH)(μ3-OH)4(L1)(acac)6]·3CH2Cl2·CH3OH·H2O; empirical C74H103Cl6Ho5O23S4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
